WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.569
Lost authenticator:
recovery and MFA reset.

2
00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:09.499
Use a saved recovery code, understand
one-use codes, and enroll again after an

3
00:00:09.499 --> 00:00:11.800
administrator resets MFA.

4
00:00:13.399 --> 00:00:18.743
If you lose the MERIT entry in your
authenticator, start with your user name

5
00:00:18.743 --> 00:00:20.690
and password as usual.

6
00:00:21.726 --> 00:00:24.395
Choose Can't access your authenticator?

7
00:00:24.395 --> 00:00:26.038
to see recovery options.

8
00:00:26.038 --> 00:00:31.502
An enabled email-code option may also
be available on the previous screen.

9
00:00:31.862 --> 00:00:35.838
Enter an unused recovery
code saved during setup.

10
00:00:35.838 --> 00:00:39.570
It has ten characters;
the hyphen is optional.

11
00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:42.242
Never share a recovery code.

12
00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:45.287
Choose Use recovery code and sign in.

13
00:00:45.287 --> 00:00:51.080
A successful recovery code signs you in
once; it does not repair or replace your

14
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.494
authenticator.

15
00:00:52.846 --> 00:00:55.729
A used code cannot work a second time.

16
00:00:55.729 --> 00:01:01.211
If it is rejected, use another
unused code or ask for an MFA reset.

17
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:14.103
Contact your agency's MERIT administrator
or help desk through your usual support

18
00:01:14.103 --> 00:01:15.103
channel.

19
00:01:15.103 --> 00:01:18.015
Give your user name and
explain what you lost.

20
00:01:18.315 --> 00:01:21.406
Ask them to verify your
identity and reset MFA.

21
00:01:21.406 --> 00:01:26.602
Administrators need another administrator;
platform administrators need another

22
00:01:26.602 --> 00:01:28.515
platform administrator.

23
00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:34.284
An MFA reset ends active sessions and
invalidates old authenticator and recovery

24
00:01:34.284 --> 00:01:35.284
codes.

25
00:01:35.284 --> 00:01:39.206
Wait for your administrator to
confirm it before restarting.

26
00:01:39.506 --> 00:01:45.062
After the confirmed reset, choose Sign in
again after an MFA reset and enter your

27
00:01:45.062 --> 00:01:46.062
password.

28
00:01:46.062 --> 00:01:49.643
MERIT asks you to set up
a new authenticator entry.

29
00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:54.284
Add the new MERIT entry to your
app, verify its current code,

30
00:01:54.284 --> 00:01:56.562
and save the new recovery codes.

31
00:01:56.562 --> 00:01:59.667
Use the new entry for future sign-ins.

32
00:02:00.831 --> 00:02:06.395
In this video you used a one-use recovery
code, identified the support path when no

33
00:02:06.395 --> 00:02:10.885
codes remain, and enrolled again
after a confirmed MFA reset.
